    "stem": "Sonia builds a Sierpinski Carpet. After step $2$ she has $H_{2} = 9$ holes and $R_{2} = 64$ remaining squares. At the next step every remaining square gains one new centre hole, and old holes stay.\n\nHow many holes are there at step $3$?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "$64$, counting the remaining squares as if they were the holes.",
      "B": "$64$, adding only the new holes and forgetting the $9$ old holes.",
      "C": "$73$, because $H_{3} = H_{2} + R_{2} = 9 + 64$.",
      "D": "$137$, by also counting the $64$ filled remaining squares as holes."
    },
